---
import ProjectLayout  from '@/layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import ProjectSection from '@/components/ProjectSection.astro';
import ProjectGallery from '@/components/ProjectGallery.astro';
import SpecTable      from '@/components/SpecTable.astro';
import { getProject, getNeighbours } from '@/data/projects';

const p = getProject('robotics-techforge');
---

<ProjectLayout
  title={p.title}
  subtitle="Team & Community"
  role={p.role}
  year={p.year}
  tags={p.tags}
  overview={p.summary}
  ogImage={p.cover}
  specs={[
    { key: 'Students taught', value: '20+'     },
    { key: 'Team growth',     value: '25%'     },
    { key: 'Raised',          value: '~$5,000' },
    { key: 'Summer camps',    value: '2 years' },
  ]}
  {...getNeighbours(p.slug)}
>

  <ProjectSection num="01" title="TechForge" dark>
    <p>
      I co-founded <strong>TechForge</strong>, Bishop Feehan's hands-on design
      and fabrication club, open to every student in grades 9–12. It exists
      because the gap between wanting to build something and being allowed near
      the machines that build it is mostly a gap in teaching.
    </p>
    <p>
      The club works in 3D printing, CNC machining and drone technology. I have
      personally taught more than twenty students to use printers, CNC
      machines, hand tools and CAD — not demonstrations, but enough that they
      can start a part of their own and finish it.
    </p>

    <h3>What the club has built</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/research/tactile-learning-tiles">Tactile learning tiles</a> for
        children with disabilities, donated to Pappas Rehabilitation Hospital
      </li>
      <li>
        A working <a href="/research/santa-shop-conveyor">conveyor</a> carrying
        3D-printed toys for the school's annual Santa Shop
      </li>
    </ul>

    <ProjectGallery
      cols={2}
      images={[
        {
          src: '/images/projects/santa-team.webp',
          alt: 'The TechForge team gathered around the conveyor in the school fabrication lab, watching it run',
          caption: 'The team watching the conveyor run for the first time at full length.',
        },
        {
          src: '/images/projects/tactile-tiles.webp',
          alt: 'Finished tactile learning tiles with raised icons, large print and braille',
          caption: 'Tactile tiles, designed and printed by the club and donated to Pappas Rehabilitation Hospital.',
        },
      ]}
    />
  </ProjectSection>

  <ProjectSection num="02" title="Robotics, as captain">
    <p>
      Captaining the robotics team turned out to be less about robots than
      about the conditions a team needs before it can build one: knowing what
      parts you own, having a budget, and having enough people.
    </p>

    <SpecTable
      caption="What changed"
      rows={[
        { key: 'Membership',   value: 'Grew the team by 25% in a single year' },
        { key: 'Organization', value: 'Instituted a cataloguing and repair system for team components' },
        { key: 'Budget',       value: 'Took on planning and ordering; secured a $1,000 increase from my ISEF winnings' },
        { key: 'Fundraising',  value: 'Built the case that raised close to $5,000 for a Bambu Lab H2C in the school fabrication lab' },
        { key: 'Teaching',     value: 'Building, 3D printing, CNC, CAD, tool use and design, to 20+ students' },
        { key: 'Outreach',     value: 'Two years volunteering at the robotics summer camp, teaching FIRST and FTC to elementary and middle schoolers' },
      ]}
    />

    <p>
      The printer is the part I am most pleased with. I put together the
      presentation that justified it, and it now sits in the school's
      fabrication lab where any student can use it — which is considerably
      more useful than one more thing in my own workshop.
    </p>

    <ProjectGallery
      cols={1}
      ratio="16 / 9"
      images={[
        {
          alt: 'The robotics team at work in the fabrication lab',
          pending: 'Photo to come — robotics team',
        },
      ]}
    />
  </ProjectSection>

  <ProjectSection num="03" title="Mentoring beyond school" dark>
    <p>
      I mentor science fair students for free, at Bishop Feehan and online
      through LinkedIn, Discord and Zoom. Most of what I pass on is not
      technical: it is how to choose a question you can actually answer, how to
      keep records good enough to defend, and what judges are listening for.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also sit on the <strong>Massachusetts Science &amp; Engineering Fair
      Advisory Board</strong>, helping plan the fairs and the interaction
      between current students and alumni.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are a student working on a project and want a second opinion on
      it, <a href="/contact">get in touch</a> — this part is free and I mean it.
    </p>
  </ProjectSection>

</ProjectLayout>
